<ol class="ltx_toclist ltx_toclist_subsection">
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1" title="In 4.1 Contextual Influences Substantially Shift Preferences ‣ 4 Results ‣ Moral Preferences of LLMs Under Directed Contextual Influence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Different contexts have qualitatively different effects.</span></a></li>
</ol></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#S4.SS2" title="In 4 Results ‣ Moral Preferences of LLMs Under Directed Contextual Influence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">4.2 </span>Influences Can Backfire Despite Attempted Neutrality</span></a>
<ol class="ltx_toclist ltx_toclist_subsection">
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1" title="In 4.2 Influences Can Backfire Despite Attempted Neutrality ‣ 4 Results ‣ Moral Preferences of LLMs Under Directed Contextual Influence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Backfiring rates are higher when models have significant baseline preferences.</span></a></li>
</ol></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#S4.SS3" title="In 4 Results ‣ Moral Preferences of LLMs Under Directed Contextual Influence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">4.3 </span>Steerability Asymmetry is Not Easily Predictable from Baseline Preferences</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#S4.SS4" title="In 4 Results ‣ Moral Preferences of LLMs Under Directed Contextual Influence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">4.4 </span>Reasoning Makes Models More Utilitarian and Shifts Sensitivities</span></a>
<ol class="ltx_toclist ltx_toclist_subsection">
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S4.SS4.SSS0.Px1" title="In 4.4 Reasoning Makes Models More Utilitarian and Shifts Sensitivities ‣ 4 Results ‣ Moral Preferences of LLMs Under Directed Contextual Influence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">With reasoning, models predominantly (97%) pick the larger group when no influence is present</span></a></li>
