<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Additional Experimental Results</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section presents aggregate statistics by influence type (<a href="#A3.SS1" title="C.1 Results by Influence Type ‣ Appendix C Additional Experimental Results ‣ Moral Preferences of LLMs Under Directed Contextual Influence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>), by demographic factor (<a href="#A3.SS2" title="C.2 Results by Demographic Factor ‣ Appendix C Additional Experimental Results ‣ Moral Preferences of LLMs Under Directed Contextual Influence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a>), and by model (<a href="#A3.SS3" title="C.3 Results by Model ‣ Appendix C Additional Experimental Results ‣ Moral Preferences of LLMs Under Directed Contextual Influence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.3</span></a>). We also provide breakdowns by reasoning condition (<a href="#A3.SS4" title="C.4 Results by Reasoning Condition ‣ Appendix C Additional Experimental Results ‣ Moral Preferences of LLMs Under Directed Contextual Influence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.4</span></a>) and detailed results for specific model-factor combinations in GPT 5.2 (<a href="#A3.SS7" title="C.7 Detailed Results for GPT-5.2 ‣ Appendix C Additional Experimental Results ‣ Moral Preferences of LLMs Under Directed Contextual Influence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.7</span></a>). We also analysed invalid response rates (<a href="#A3.SS8" title="C.8 Invalid Responses ‣ Appendix C Additional Experimental Results ‣ Moral Preferences of LLMs Under Directed Contextual Influence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.8</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Results by Influence Type</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#A3.T3" title="In C.1 Results by Influence Type ‣ Appendix C Additional Experimental Results ‣ Moral Preferences of LLMs Under Directed Contextual Influence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> presents aggregate statistics for each type of contextual influence, averaged across all models, factors, and reasoning conditions. Few-shot examples produce the largest effects on average, while weak evidence produces the smallest. Notably, survey claims and weak evidence exhibit high backfire rates (31.7% and 40.9%, respectively).</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A3.T3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 3</span>: </span><span id="A3.T3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Aggregate statistics by type of contextual influence<span id="A3.T3.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">, over all factors and models (with and without reasoning).
We show averages for contextual effect (Effect), steerability (Steer), steerability asymmetry (Asym) and normalized steerability asymmetry (N-Asym). Vertical bars indicate that absolute values were taken before averaging. We also show the fraction of conditions with significant context effects (Sig) and the fraction of conditions with significant backfiring of contextual influences (BF). Backfiring rates are stated as percentage of cases with significant effects.</span></span></figcaption>
<table id="A3.T3.6" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A3.T3.6.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A3.T3.6.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><span id="A3.T3.6.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps" style="font-size:90%;">Influence Type</span></th>
<th id="A3.T3.6.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><math id="A3.T3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo fence="false" maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">|</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.T3.6.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps" style="font-size:90%;">Effect<math id="A3.T3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|</annotation></semantics></math></span></th>
<th id="A3.T3.6.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><math id="A3.T3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo fence="false" maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">|</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.T3.6.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps" style="font-size:90%;">Steer<math id="A3.T3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|</annotation></semantics></math></span></th>
<th id="A3.T3.6.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="A3.T3.6.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps" style="font-size:90%;">Sig</span></th>
<th id="A3.T3.6.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="A3.T3.6.1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps" style="font-size:90%;">BF</span></th>
<th id="A3.T3.6.1.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><math id="A3.T3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo fence="false" maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">|</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.T3.6.1.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps" style="font-size:90%;">Asym<math id="A3.T3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|</annotation></semantics></math></span></th>
<th id="A3.T3.6.1.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><math id="A3.T3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo fence="false" maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">|</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.T3.6.1.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps" style="font-size:90%;">N-Asym<math id="A3.T3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|</annotation></semantics></math></span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A3.T3.6.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A3.T3.6.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t"><span id="A3.T3.6.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps" style="font-size:90%;">survey</span></th>
<td id="A3.T3.6.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><span id="A3.T3.6.2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps" style="font-size:90%;">0.11</span></td>
